<title>ITALY: NORDIC-RESULTS OF WORLD CUP RELAY RACES.</title>
<headline>NORDIC-RESULTS OF WORLD CUP RELAY RACES.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSON, Italy 1996-12-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Results of the World Cup</p>
<p>Nordic cross-country relays on Sunday:</p>
<p>Men's 4X10km classic:</p>
<p> 1. Norway    (Egil Kristiansen, Anders Eide, Kristen Skjeldal,</p>
<p>    Bjorn Daehlie)	 one hour, 34 minutes, 50.3 seconds</p>
<p> 2. Italy     (Maurizio Pozzi, Fulvio Valbusa, Gaudenzio Godioz</p>
<p>    Silvio Fauner)				1:35:02.3</p>
<p> 3. Sweden    (Mathias Fredriksson, Anders Bergstroem, Niklas</p>
<p>    Jonsson, Torgny Mogren)		   1:35:05.8</p>
<p> 4. Russia    (Grigorij Gutnikov, Sergei Tshepikov, Vladmir</p>
<p>    Legotin, Alexej Prokurorov)	     1:35:49.8</p>
<p> 5. Finland   (Sami Repo, Mika Myllyla, Jukka Hartonen, Jari</p>
<p>    Isometsa)				     1:36:10.1</p>
<p> 6. Austria   (Christoph Sumann, Christian Hoffmann, Gerhard</p>
<p>    Urain, Achim Walcher)		     1:36:44.3</p>
<p> 7. Slovakia  (Ivan Batory, Martin Bajcicak, Andrej Paricka</p>
<p>    Ivan Hudac)				   1:37:00.8</p>
<p> 8. Czech    (Lubos Buchia, Petr Michl, Vaclav Korunka, Josef</p>
<p>Kucera)					     1:37:11.8</p>
<p> 9. Italy III (Christian Zorzi, Sergio Piller, Gianantonio</p>
<p>    Zanetel, Klaus Mariotti)		  1:37:19.9</p>
<p> 10. Italy IV</p>
<p>(Giorgio Di Cenia, Fabio May, Fabio Santus,</p>
<p>    Roberto De Zolt)			    1:37:28.3</p>
<p>Women's 4X5km classic</p>
<p> 1. Russia     (Nina Gavriliuk, Olga Danilova, Liubov</p>
<p>    Egorova, Elena Vaelbe)	   51 minutes, 42.9 seconds</p>
<p> 2. Russia II  (Olga Korneva, Svetlana Nageikina, Larissa</p>
<p>    Lazutina, Julija Tschepalova)	     52:10.8</p>
<p> 3. Italy	(Gabriella Paruzzi, Sabina Valbusa, Guidina</p>
<p>    Dai Sasso, Stefania Belmondo)	     52:38.2</p>
<p> 4. France     (Sophie Villeneuve, Karine Philippot, Ann-</p>
<p>    Laure Condevaux, Annick Pierel)	   53:20.2</p>
<p> 5. Norway     (Anita Moen-Guidon, Eva Kjerstadmo, Majhelen</p>
<p>    Sorkmo, Trude Dybendahl)		    53:34.1</p>
<p> 6. Germany    (Anke Schulze, Constanze Blum, Kati Wilhelm</p>
<p>    Corinna May)				    53:35.2</p>
<p> 7. Sweden     (Anna Frithioff, Annika Evaldsson, Sara Hugg</p>
<p>    Ek Elin)					  54:00.6</p>
<p> 8. Switzerland (Sylvia Honegger, Brigitte Albrecht, Natascia</p>
<p>    Leonardi, Nadia Scaruffi)		   54:29.2</p>
<p> 9. Japan	(Kumiko Yokoyama, Kumiko Auki, Sumiko Yokoyoma</p>
<p>    Tomoni Ootaka)				  54:40.4</p>
<p> 10. Finland</p>
<p>(Kerttu Tiikkainen, Kati Pulkkinen, Riikka</p>
<p>    Sirvioe, Kati Sundqvist)		     55:13.2</p>
